            },
            "reviewBody": "I don't add any sugar. The pineapple is sweet enough. Really good.",
            "datePublished": "2023-05-22T13:43:34.311Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nancy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I thought why the sugar, so after reading the reviews, I decided to cut the sugar to 1/4 c., added one medium onion diced and 1 teaspoon crushed red pepper flakes. I still thought they were sweet, as I served it on King’s Hawaiian buns. I will make them again and eliminate all sugar. I think I will still cook the pineapple to eliminate the remaining juice after draining.",
            "datePublished": "2020-07-09T00:02:02.457Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jennifer Renee S"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really liked the cream cheese spread. It reminds me of the really good honey almond shmear at Einstein Bagels. I think the spread alone would be really good on a bagel. My mom thought it would be really good just on ham. The sandwich may be better with an open-faced sandwich, so it had less bread or maybe more of the insides. I'm not sure, but it was still really good.",
            "datePublished": "2019-09-16T17:04:41.370Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jane"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved it as-is, but I could also see making this with cubed ham or even chicken for finger sandwiches!",
            "datePublished": "2016-04-02T14:23:16.743Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jennifer Baker"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love the concept of this sandwich because my family likes ham and pineapple together. As written, the cream cheese pineapple mixture is waaaay too sweet, and I didn't add the full cup of sugar (I just couldn't do it). I would make it again, but would decrease the sugar by half or more. My 9 year old loved it though, but it was because it tasted so sweet.",
            "datePublished": "2012-02-21T16:43:11.890Z"
          }
